# Time-boxed risk acceptances for the production image scan.
# Policy: ignore-unfixed stays "false" in CI; every entry here must name one
# CVE, carry an expiry (Trivy re-fails the gate automatically after it), and
# have a matching residual-risk entry in docs/THREAT_MODEL.md.

# OpenSSL QUIC *server* unbounded-memory DoS in Debian 13 libssl3t64
# (3.5.6-1~deb13u2). No fixed Debian package exists yet. Not reachable in
# this image: the only processes are Node 24 services, and Node does not
# enable OpenSSL's QUIC server APIs. Re-evaluate before the expiry; remove
# the moment Debian ships a fix. Accepted 2026-08-23 (pending founder
# review; recorded in the session brief).
CVE-2026-14456 exp:2026-10-15
